section.para:
      If you have an Apple Silicon computer, type:
      % mkdir -p &install.prefix;
% cd &install.prefix;
% curl -LO &macarm64.url;
% tar -zxf &macarm64.file;
      If you have an older Intel computer, type:
      % mkdir -p &install.prefix;
% cd &install.prefix;
% curl -LO &macintel64.url;
% tar -zxf &macintel64.file;
      Check that the executable runs:
      % ~/Applications/bali-phy-&version;/bin/bali-phy --version
      You still need to add it to your PATH as described in .

      Then download and extract the executables.  For Ubuntu 24.04 on x86-64, type:
      % mkdir -p &install.prefix;
% cd &install.prefix;
% wget &ubuntu2404.url;
% tar -zxf &ubuntu2404.file;
      For Ubuntu 26.04 on x86-64, type:
      % mkdir -p &install.prefix;
% cd &install.prefix;
% wget &ubuntu2604.url;
% tar -zxf &ubuntu2604.file;
      Second, check that the executable runs:
      % ~/Applications/bali-phy-&version;/bin/bali-phy --version

See  for details of the output files and
         for optional programs to inspect trees, alignments,
        and parameter traces.
